---
title: Sequence diagram - sign in
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant W as Web portal<br/>Login.jsx, lib/auth.js, lib/api.js
    participant RL as Rate limiter<br/>auth-strict, 5 per min per IP
    participant AC as AuthController
    participant AS as AuthService
    participant PH as PasswordHasherService
    participant TS as TokenService
    participant RT as InMemoryRefreshTokenStore
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>User table

    U->>W: email + password, Sign in
    W->>W: client-side checks (email format, required)
    W->>RL: POST /api/auth/login {email, password}
    alt more than 5 requests this minute from this IP
        RL-->>W: 429 Too Many Requests
        W-->>U: "Too many attempts, wait a minute"
    else within limit
        RL->>AC: Login(LoginRequest)
        alt model invalid (email format, password under 6 chars)
            AC-->>W: 400 ApiErrorResponse {message, errors[]}
            W-->>U: field errors
        else model valid
            AC->>AS: LoginAsync(request)
            AS->>DB: CanConnectAsync, then SELECT user by lower(email)
            DB-->>AS: User or null
            opt database unreachable or user not in DB
                AS->>AS: fall back to 4 built-in seed users
            end
            alt no user, IsActive false or EmailConfirmed false
                AS-->>AC: null
                AC-->>W: 401 "Invalid email or password."
                W-->>U: generic sign-in error
            else user found
                AS->>PH: VerifyPassword(password, hash) BCrypt
                alt wrong password
                    PH-->>AS: false
                    AS-->>AC: null
                    AC-->>W: 401 "Invalid email or password."
                    W-->>U: generic sign-in error
                else correct password
                    PH-->>AS: true
                    AS->>TS: GenerateAccessToken(user) JWT HS256, 60 min
                    AS->>TS: GenerateRefreshToken() 64 random bytes
                    AS->>RT: SaveTokenAsync(refresh token, expires 7 days)
                    AS-->>AC: AuthResponse
                    AC-->>W: 200 {accessToken, tokenExpiry, refreshToken, role, displayName, userId}
                    W->>W: access token in memory, refresh token in sessionStorage
                    W-->>U: redirect to role home (/admin, /consultant or /client)
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Note over W,AC: When a later API call returns 401, see seq-token-refresh
